# Code owners.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners of every file a pull request
# touches. Combined with the branch protection rule "Require review from Code
# Owners", this makes the owner's approval mandatory before a merge into a
# protected branch.
#
# CODEOWNERS is read from the base branch of the pull request, not from the
# branch proposing the change. A change to this file only takes effect once it
# is merged into the branch it is meant to protect.
#
# Setup that makes this file binding: documentation/branch-protection.md

# Everything, by default.
*    @Handsomeboy990

# Authorized reviewers, added as the project grows. Uncomment and extend:
# *  @Handsomeboy990 @second-reviewer

# Per-area owners, if ownership ever needs to split. Uncomment and fill:
# /writing/        @Handsomeboy990
# /documents/      @Handsomeboy990
# /engineering/    @Handsomeboy990
# /shared/         @Handsomeboy990
# /tests/          @Handsomeboy990
# /config/         @Handsomeboy990

# These four govern the whole repository. Keep them owned by a maintainer
# whatever else is delegated.
/LICENSE             @Handsomeboy990
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @Handsomeboy990
/install.sh          @Handsomeboy990
/CLAUDE.md           @Handsomeboy990
